"answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative with varying details across different communications. It was introduced as a data analytics and cloud storage optimization project with an initial phase budget of $500,000, later adjusted to $550,000, and eventually approved for a total budget of $2 million. Key personnel include Sarah Tan, Marcus Cole, Omar Jensen, and John Doe. Milestones achieved include the completion of the testing phase and successful prototype testing for secure file sharing. The project involves several phases, including design, development, and compliance planning (with a specific $55,000 budget for compliance training and audits). Kickoff and milestone celebration dates mentioned range from June to October, with onboarding sessions for partners scheduled in April 2023."
